## Phase 8: User Story 6 - Global Filter-as-you-Type Search & URL Query Synchronization (Priority: P1)

**Goal**: Provide an instantaneous filter-as-you-type search input in the top bar that filters tasks across all views and syncs state to URL query parameter `?search=...`.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T029 [P] [US6] Add search `v-text-field` and reactive `searchQuery` ref in the top controls bar of `frontend/pages/index.vue`.
- [x] T030 [P] [US6] Integrate case-insensitive task description filtering into `filteredTasks` computed property, propagating reactively to `TaskList` and `KanbanBoard`.
- [x] T031 [US6] Implement bidirectional `?search=` URL query synchronization with 300ms debounce on typing, preserving existing query parameters.

---

## Phase 9: User Story 7 - Multi-Toggle Task Status Filtering in Task List (Priority: P1)

**Goal**: Make status filters in the Tasks list view independent toggles rather than mutually exclusive, aggregating matching tasks and synchronizing with URL query parameter `?status=...`.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T032 [P] [US7] Convert `v-btn-toggle` in `frontend/components/TaskList.vue` to `multiple` binding to `selectedStatuses` array.
- [x] T033 [P] [US7] Implement `displayedTasks` computed property to aggregate tasks matching any active status.
- [x] T034 [US7] Implement bidirectional URL query synchronization for `?status=` supporting comma-separated values (e.g. `pending,waiting`, `completed`, `none`).
- [x] T035 [US7] Update data-table headers to dynamically include `Due`, `Wait`, and `Recur` columns based on active status selections.
- [x] T036 [US7] Refactor batch action buttons (Done, Restore, Delete) and row action icons to evaluate individual `item.status`.
- [x] T036b [US7] Ensure `?status=` query parameter has no filtering effect in the Kanban view while preserving its value intact across mode switches.

---

## Phase 10: User Story 8 - Gantt Chart, Timeline Views & Calendarless Flow (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Deliver a comprehensive timeline visualization with deterministic date sequencing, priority/urgency sorting, clean orthogonal arrow routing, and calendarless topological flow view.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T037 [P] [US8] Implement horizontal task sequencing engine (start date > due date > latest precedent task end > today; length spans start through due date).
- [x] T038 [P] [US8] Implement vertical task sorting by Priority (HML), Urgency, dependent task count, and alphabetical description.
- [x] T039 [US8] Implement orthogonal SVG dependency arrow routing with dynamic lane allocation avoiding card body crossings and overlapping vertical lines.
- [x] T040 [US8] Implement multi-scale timeframes (Day, Week, Month) with fluid column sizing, horizontal scrolling, and truncation of unpopulated empty intervals.
- [x] T041 [US8] Implement Calendarless flow view displaying topological task progression starting from index 0 without calendar date columns.

